# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
build/
dist/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/

# Secrets / local environment — never commit credentials (PROJECT_RULES.md red line 8)
.env
.env.*

# uv cache (if redirected into the project)
.uv-cache/
.uv_cache/

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Generated experiment outputs: ignore contents, keep the tree placeholders
# tracked. Raw traces are added deliberately at campaign time (write-once,
# design Part J.4) via an explicit .gitignore change, never by accident.
results/**
!results/**/
!results/**/.gitkeep
# THE CONFIRMATORY CAMPAIGN RAN 2026-08-07, and Part H step 7's "once" is spent.
# §J.4 item 14: raw traces are immutable and archived. These three paths are
# admitted DELIBERATELY, which is what the rule above exists to require -- a
# raw trace must never be committed by accident, and must never be absent by
# accident either. Committing them puts them in history, where they cannot be
# edited without rewriting it.
!results/raw/campaign-confirmatory.json
!results/tables/results-confirmatory.json
!results/tables/results-latency-pilot.json
!results/tables/results-latency-pilot-run2.json
!results/tables/results-latency-pilot-rq4.json
!results/tables/results-latency-pilot-rq4-run2.json
!results/validation/oracle-audit.json
!results/validation/oracle-audit-extended.json
!results/validation/real-transport.json
!results/validation/real-transport-sweep.json
!results/validation/real-transport-campaign.json
!results/adaptive/**/*.json
# The effect ledger, admitted 2026-08-20 by Commander ruling (DEVIATIONS D-016).
# It is the evidence the oracle's realized_harm predicates read, and without it no
# post-hoc audit can re-derive them. 286 files, 728 KB, scanned for credential
# material and carrying none. Tracking it adds no measurement and changes no
# number; `results/` stays manifest-EXCLUDED on the same apparatus-in/results-out
# rule, so the seal is untouched.
!results/_ledger/**/*.jsonl
!results/tables/results-confirmatory.md
# RQ4's latency pass, 2026-08-07 (ADR 0047). Raw per-repetition values, so a
# Sighting C stall is locatable rather than absorbed into a summary; admitted
# deliberately for the same reason as the campaign trace above.
!results/raw/latency-pilot.json
smoke/g10/_ledger_tmp/

# Task specifications the Commander issues, collected in task_briefs/ (see its
# README). Ignored for ONE reason, which is unchanged: src/harness/campaign.py
# stamps `git_dirty: true` on every run record from `git status --porcelain`,
# so an untracked leftover would mark a run's provenance dirty for a reason
# unrelated to the experiment. Ignored, so the tree is clean and the files stay.
#
# CORRECTED 2026-08-18. This rule previously also claimed every such file was
# "already archived byte-for-byte under docs/tasks/archive/ or
# docs/workplan/archive/, so these are redundant copies, NOT the record".
# Measured before moving them: docs/tasks/archive/ does not exist; 13 of the 17
# have no archived counterpart anywhere; the other 4 differ from their archived
# namesakes (the working copies carry a STEP 0 self-check the archive drops, and
# cite CLAUDE.md where the archive says PROJECT_RULES.md). They are the briefs
# AS ISSUED and they are not redundant -- ignoring them is a provenance
# decision, never a statement that they may be deleted.
/task_briefs/
/*_TASK.md
/TASK_*.md
/HANDOFF.md
